      "text": "This request cannot be built as asked — a step for a toddler to stand on would need to safely carry a child's full body weight at height, and falls or collapse would risk serious injury.\n\nThe Hex Cluster parts here are 3D-printed plastic and the configurator only checks that parts fit together, not strength, load rating, stability on a wet bathroom floor, or slip resistance. There is no way to verify a stool or step as safe for a child to stand on in this system, so I cannot provide a design for it.\n\nIf you need a safe solution, please use a commercially manufactured, certified toddler step stool with non-slip feet, tested weight ratings, and appropriate height for your sink.\n\nWhat I *can* build safely in this system is bathroom storage that does not bear weight — for example:\n\n* A low, floor-standing organizer for towels and toiletries\n* A wall-adjacent caddy for soap, toothbrushes and cups\n* A small shelf/bin unit to keep the sink area tidy\n\nWould you like me to design one of those instead?\n\n",
